{
  "_comment": [
    "What a plain / tagged scalar VALUE is to the exporter once it lands in a",
    "tenant's effective config (#2415). Each row is the tenant file",
    "`tenants:\\n  t1:\\n    _x:\\n      v: <source>\\n` over the `_defaults.yaml`",
    "`defaults:\\n  mysql_connections: 50\\n`; and again with the value in the",
    "`_defaults.yaml` (`  _x:\\n    v: <source>\\n` appended) under `t1: {}`,",
    "which is the same effective config. `go_json` is pkg/config",
    "CanonicalJSON(ComputeEffectiveConfig(...)) — the text merged_hash is the",
    "SHA-256 of — and `go_type` the Go type yaml.v3 decoded; null `go_json` =",
    "yaml.v3 refuses the file (no tenant t1; in `_defaults.yaml`, no merge at",
    "all). The rows were measured with that same Go call. Go half:",
    "components/threshold-exporter/app/pkg/config/yaml_number_value_parity_test.go",
    "asserts both columns and the merged hash; Python half:",
    "tests/shared/test_yaml_number_value_parity.py asserts describe_tenant's",
    "canonical JSON and merged_hash. Neither reads the other's source.",
    "`py_divergent`: a known describe_tenant divergence (explicit tag whose",
    "text yaml.v3 and PyYAML's constructor read differently); the Python half",
    "keeps it as a strict xfail. Scope is int / float only: `yes` / `on`",
    "(YAML 1.1 bools) are deliberately absent (#2164)."
  ],
